00:02:55.000 --> 00:03:27.000
Sometimes called motivational incentives is another term that we often use to describe contingency management. And, you know, psychologists developed a long time ago, the idea of operating conditioning. So that's the classic idea of sort of positive reinforcement. And positive reinforcement really is what contingency management. management's all about. So that's the idea that if you want to help somebody change the behavior, you want to increase a behavior or maintain it in the long run, the best way to do it, the most effective way to do it, is with reinforcers or what we more commonly call a reward.
